  numbered rows whose attachment is not dated after the paper it sits in (checked, not reported):
    frus1872p2v2 row line 5485: No. 13. |  | Transmits reply of Earl Granville of March 20th to Mr. Fish’s instructions of 27th ultimo, to him, (General Schenck,) and printed memorandum in three parts. His note treats upon incidental or consequential damages. Reviews the Johnson-Clarendon Treaty. Part 1 of the memorandum treats “on the waiver of claims for indirect losses contained in the 36th Protocol.” Part 2, “on the construction of the Treaty of Washington.” Part 3, “on the amount of the claims for indirect losses.” General Schenck, in reply, states that he will forward the above to his Government without delay | p. 435; attachment "Earl Granville to General Schenck." (1872-03-20) inside d148 (1872-03-21)
    frus1876 row line 7037: No. 90 | The Emperor William to the President. | June 9 | p. 173; attachment "The Emperor William to the President." (1876-06-09) inside d91 (1876-06-29)
    frus1880 row line 14556: No. 529 | Mr. Evarts to Mr. Christiancy. | do | p. 837; attachment "Mr. Evarts to Señor Calderon." (1880-03-01) inside d528 (1880-03-01)
    frus1887 row line 11244: No. 316 | Mr. White to Mr. Bayard (No. 478). | Mar. 26 | p. 468; attachment "The Marquis of Salisbury to Mr. White" (1887-03-26) inside d316 (1887-03-30)
